@*
    A POLITE ANNOUNCEMENT THAT IS SAID AGAIN WHEN IT REPEATS - story 2.8, AC14; UX-DR25, UX-DR38; deferred-work.md:489, :549;
    open question 6 (b).

    A live region announces a CHANGE to its content. One region given the same sentence twice in a row ("Task added.", then
    "Task added.") does not change, so assistive technology says nothing the second time. This component keeps TWO polite
    regions and writes each sentence into the one that does not hold the last, clearing the other in the same render: every
    sentence is new text in an empty region, whatever was said before it. Both regions are empty from the first render
    (story 2.3's rule), so the first sentence is announced too.

    Why two regions, not one cleared and written a render later (open question 6 (a)): Blazor may apply the clearing render
    and the writing render in one browser task, which the accessibility tree can coalesce into "no change"; two regions do
    not depend on timing at all.

    The owner says a sentence by setting Text and bumping Sequence; a Sequence it has seen is never said again, and a null
    Text clears both regions (a purge).
*@

<p class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite">@_texts[0]</p>
<p class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite">@_texts[1]</p>

@code {
    private readonly string?[] _texts = new string?[2];
    private int _seen;
    private int _current = 1;

    /// <summary>The sentence to say, or <c>null</c> to clear.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Text { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Bumped by the owner each time it says <see cref="Text"/>, the same sentence again included.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Sequence { get; set; }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (Sequence == _seen)
        {
            return;
        }

        _seen = Sequence;

        if (Text is null)
        {
            _texts[0] = null;
            _texts[1] = null;
            return;
        }

        _current = 1 - _current;
        _texts[_current] = Text;
        _texts[1 - _current] = null;
    }
}
